    "result": "Perfect! All tests are now passing. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Fixed Issues\n\n### 1. **Governance module export** (`src/finetune/index.js`)\n   - Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`\n   - The test was trying to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only available in the default export\n   - Kept the default export intact for backward compatibility\n\n### 2. **Toxicity metric signature** (`src/eval/metrics.js`)\n   - Changed `toxicityMetric(outputs, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)` to `toxicityMetric(outputs, references)`\n   - The `runEvaluations` function calls metrics with `(outputs, references)`, but `toxicityMetric` was expecting banned terms as the second parameter\n   - This caused the references array to be incorrectly treated as banned terms, resulting in incorrect scoring\n   - Fixed by using `defaultBannedTerms` internally and accepting the `references` parameter (unused) to match the interface\n\n**Result**: All 28 tests across 8 test files are now passing \u2713",
